 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "In the storage room, Timur presides over the kitchen vote while standing right inside the voting booth. After accepting a discreet cash bribe, Timur looks the other way and announces that Senya has won the election seven to three.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Но это же тайное голосование.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Иди отсюда, позови сюда следующего.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Добрый день, у меня вопрос.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Независимый наблюдатель может не наблюдать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Нет, так делать совсем нельзя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Понятно, а если вот так?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Отлично, теперь ты честно проголосовал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Подводим итоги нашей честной борьбы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Сегодня в выборах победил Арсений!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Как это он вдруг победил?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "У кого-нибудь есть сейчас возражения?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Можете забирать бюллетени на салат.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Но это же тайное голосование.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But this is a secret vote, after all.' The grammar packs 'but' and 'voting' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Иди отсюда, позови сюда следующего.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Go on out of here, call the next person in.' The meaning hinges on 'go' working together with 'next' in spoken Russian. Senya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Добрый день, у меня вопрос.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Good afternoon, I have a question.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'good' and 'day' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Независимый наблюдатель может не наблюдать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Can the independent observer not watch?' Senya anchors the line on 'independent', while 'to observe' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Нет, так делать совсем нельзя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, one cannot do that at all.' Notice how Russian expresses 'no' and 'one must not' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Senya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Понятно, а если вот так?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Understood, and what if like this?' Senya anchors the line on 'understood', while 'so' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Отлично, теперь ты честно проголосовал.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Great, now you have voted fairly.' The grammar packs 'perfectly' and 'voted' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Подводим итоги нашей честной борьбы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let us sum up the results of our fair contest.' Timur anchors the line on 'we sum up', while 'struggle' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Сегодня в выборах победил Арсений!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Today Arseny won the election!' The grammar packs 'tonight' and 'Arseny' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Как это он вдруг победил?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'How did he suddenly win like that?' Fedya anchors the line on 'how', while 'won' completes the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "У кого-нибудь есть сейчас возражения?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Does anyone have any objections right now?' Timur raises the pitch on 'objections' to turn the phrase into a direct spoken question.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "timur",
   "t": "Можете забирать бюллетени на салат.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You can take the ballots for salad.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'can' and finishing on 'salad'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
